{#
    Programme page: the solution cards.

    These previously held copy and claims in the template: named client projects,
    product marks and links to anchors that do not exist on the page. That broke
    the project's rule that no visitor-facing string is hard-coded, and it stated
    facts about GDC that nothing here can substantiate.

    The section now renders from the "training.solutions" rows. The heading comes
    from a block, and each card is a row, so the copy is edited in the admin and
    the section disappears when it has no rows.

    A row that names a destination gets a link; a row without one is a plain
    card, so an editor can publish a card before the page it points at exists.
#}
{% set section = blocks['training.solutions']|default(null) %}
{% set cards = items['training.solutions']|default([]) %}

{% if cards|length > 0 %}
    <section class="ui-section" id="solutions">
        {% if section and section.heading %}
            <h2 class="ui-type-headline">{{ section.heading }}</h2>
        {% endif %}
        {% if section and section.body %}
            <p class="ui-type-body mt-4 max-w-measure">{{ section.body }}</p>
        {% endif %}

        <div class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
            {% for card in cards %}
                {% set href = gdc_link(card.linkTarget) %}
                {% include '_partials/_bento_card.html.twig' with {
                    span: loop.first ? 'md:col-span-2' : '',
                    eyebrow: card.subtitle,
                    title: card.title,
                    body: card.body,
                    cta: href ? card.linkLabel,
                    href: href,
                } only %}
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </section>
{% endif %}
